# 1. JpaRepository ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐

## Why was it introduced?

Without Spring Data JPA:

```java
entityManager.persist(product);

entityManager.find(Product.class, id);

entityManager.remove(product);
```

A lot of repetitive code.

Spring Data JPA introduced repositories to eliminate boilerplate.

---

## Definition

`JpaRepository` is a Spring Data interface that provides ready-made CRUD operations on entities.

Example

```java
public interface ProductRepository
        extends JpaRepository<Product, Long> {

}
```

Now you automatically get:

```java
save()

findById()

findAll()

delete()

count()

existsById()
```

without writing any implementation.

---

# Internal Working

```
Your Repository Interface

↓

Spring Data JPA

↓

Creates Proxy Class

↓

Uses EntityManager

↓

Hibernate

↓

Database
```

Notice:

You never implement

```java
ProductRepository
```

Spring creates it dynamically using **proxies**.

We'll learn proxy internals in Module 7.

