# @Transactional ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐

One of the most asked Spring annotations.

---

## Why Transactions?

Imagine money transfer.

```
Deduct Money

↓

Server Crash

↓

Credit Never Happens
```

Money disappears.

Very bad.

Transactions ensure:

**All operations succeed or all fail.**

---

# ACID (Interview Basic)

Know the full form.

| Property | Meaning |
|----------|---------|
| Atomicity | All or Nothing |
| Consistency | Valid State |
| Isolation | Transactions don't interfere |
| Durability | Data survives failures |

No need to memorize textbook definitions.

Understand the idea.

---

# Example

```java
@Transactional

public void transfer(){

    debit();

    credit();

}
```

If

```
credit()

fails
```

Hibernate rolls back everything.

No partial update.

---

# Internal Transaction Flow

```
@Transactional

↓

Spring Proxy

↓

Open Transaction

↓

Execute Method

↓

Success?

↓

YES

↓

Commit

-----------------

NO

↓

Rollback
```

Interview Tip:

Spring implements `@Transactional` using **AOP Proxies**, not by modifying your code directly.

We'll cover proxy internals in Module 7.

